01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
The Blind Side is a 2009 American biographical sports drama
film written and directed by John Lee Hancock.

11
01:18:50,000 --> 01:18:56,000
Based on the 2006 book of the same name by Michael Lewis, the film tells the story of Michael Oher, a football offensive lineman who
overcame an impoverished upbringing to play in the National Football League (NFL) with the help of Leigh Anne and Sean Tuohy.

12
01:26:00,000 --> 01:26:06,000
It stars Sandra Bullock as Leigh Anne, Tim McGraw
as Sean, and Quinton Aaron as Oher.

13
01:33:10,000 --> 01:33:16,000
The film was a commercial success, grossing $309
million on a $29 million budget.

14
01:40:20,000 --> 01:40:26,000
Despite mixed reviews from critics, Bullock's performance was universally praised, leading to her winning the Academy Award for Best Actress, the Golden Globe
Award for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama, and the Screen Actors Guild Award for Outstanding Performance by a Female Actor in a Leading Role.

15
01:47:30,000 --> 01:47:36,000
The film was the subject of controversy in 2023 when Oher alleged the Tuohys tricked him into signing a conservatorship agreement
instead of legally adopting him, which prevented him from receiving royalties while the family indirectly made millions.

16
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:46,000
The film explores themes of sports, american football,
adoption, private school, education.

